{"id":"sr-2-veresk","slug":"sr-2-veresk","name":"SR-2 Veresk","aliases":["SR2 Veresk","SM-2 Veresk","Veresk submachine gun","Veresk (submachine gun)"],"kind":"firearm","category":"pdws","subcategory":"Submachine gun","description":"The SR-2 \"Veresk\" (Russian: СР-2 «Вереск», English: Heather) is a Russian submachine gun designed to fire the 9×21mm Gyurza pistol cartridge.","history":"Development of a new submachine gun chambered for the 9×21mm Gyurza cartridge (also used by the SR-1 \"Vektor\" pistol) was launched in the mid-1990s on the request of Russia's Federal Security Service (FSB).\nA weapon was presented in 1999, developed by TsNIITochMash in Klimovsk, which received the designation of SR-2 (Russian: Специальная Разработка 2, romanized: Spetsial′naya Razrabotka 2, English: Special Development 2) and nicknamed \"Veresk\" (\"Heather\").\n\"Veresk\" and its round were created as a compact weapon capable of engaging enemies wearing Russian class-II body armor (able to stop ordinary pistol bullets, such as 9×19mm Parabellum and 7.62×25mm Tokarev), and soft-skinned vehicles, at distances up to 200 metres.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Cartridge & Action","items":[{"label":"Cartridge","value":"9×21mm Gyurza"},{"label":"Action","value":"Gas-operated, rotating bolt"},{"label":"Rate of Fire","value":"950 rounds/min","numeric":950,"unit":"rounds/min"},{"label":"Muzzle Velocity","value":"415–430 m/s"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"20- or 30-round detachable box magazine"},{"label":"Sights","value":"KP SR-2 reflex sight (red-dot sight)"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"1.65 kg","numeric":1.65,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Length","value":"603 mm stock extended","numeric":603,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Length","value":"367 mm stock folded","numeric":367,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Barrel Length","value":"174 mm","numeric":174,"unit":"mm"}]},{"group":"Performance","items":[{"label":"Effective Range","value":"100 m","numeric":100,"unit":"m"},{"label":"Maximum Range","value":"200 m","numeric":200,"unit":"m"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designed","value":"mid to late 1990s"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"TsNIITochMash"},{"label":"Produced","value":"1999–2005 (SR-2)"},{"label":"Produced","value":"2005–present (SR-2M)"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"Russia"},{"label":"In Service","value":"1999–present"}]}],"specIndex":{"Cartridge":"9×21mm Gyurza","Action":"Gas-operated, rotating bolt","Rate of Fire":"950 rounds/min","Muzzle Velocity":"415–430 m/s","Feed System":"20- or 30-round detachable box magazine","Sights":"KP SR-2 reflex sight (red-dot sight)","Weight":"1.65 kg","Length":"603 mm stock extended","Barrel Length":"174 mm","Effective Range":"100 m","Maximum Range":"200 m","Designed":"mid to late 1990s","Manufacturer":"TsNIITochMash","Produced":"1999–2005 (SR-2)","Origin":"Russia","In Service":"1999–present"},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/53/%D0%9F%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%82-%D0%BF%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BC%D1%91%D1%82_%D0%A1%D0%A02%D0%9C_-_%D0%A6%D0%9D%D0%98%D0%98%D0%A2%D0%9E%D0%A7%D0%9C%D0%90%D0%A8_02.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9F%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%82-%D0%BF%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BC%D1%91%D1%82_%D0%A1%D0%A02%D0%9C_-_%D0%A6%D0%9D%D0%98%D0%98%D0%A2%D0%9E%D0%A7%D0%9C%D0%90%D0%A8_02.jpg","width":2250,"height":1500,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Vitaly V. Kuzmin"},"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/%D0%9F%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%82-%D0%BF%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BC%D1%91%D1%82_%D0%A1%D0%A02%D0%9C_-_%D0%A6%D0%9D%D0%98%D0%98%D0%A2%D0%9E%D0%A7%D0%9C%D0%90%D0%A8_02.jpg/330px-%D0%9F%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%82-%D0%BF%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BC%D1%91%D1%82_%D0%A1%D0%A02%D0%9C_-_%D0%A6%D0%9D%D0%98%D0%98%D0%A2%D0%9E%D0%A7%D0%9C%D0%90%D0%A8_0